text:
Maya Chen: Quick heads-up — I pushed a tiny Next.js + LangChain sample that wires the Redwood JS SDK into our eval harness. It’s in the samplekit branch: https://git.redwood/samplekit/next-llm-hands-on. Looking for feedback on auth+retry behavior; saw weird 401 loops on SSR paths.

Samir Patel: Nice. Can you repro reliably? SSR vs Edge?

Maya Chen: Repro is reliable when session refresh happens mid-request on SSR (getServerSideProps). Edge runtime didn't show it, oddly. Sequence: token expires, SSR code calls /api/generate, SDK auto-refresh starts, concurrent requests get 401 and the SDK retry logic returns error instead of waiting for refresh.

Jordan Lee: That sounds like a race between token refresh and the request interceptor. Current JS SDK has two parity gaps vs python: no global refresh lock and retry backoff is fixed small.

Olivia Park: Can you paste the minimal example?

Maya Chen: Sure — current API usage in the sample:```js
// pages/api/generate.js
import Redwood from 'redwood-sdk'
const client = new Redwood({ apiKey: process.env.RW_KEY })
export default async function handler(req, res) {
  const out = await client.generate({ model: 'open-llama-mini', prompt: req.body.prompt })
  return res.json(out)
}
```

Maya Chen: When token is rotating the client throws 401 and doesn't attempt refresh-then-retry. Quick patch suggestion I tested locally: add a refresh lock and exponential fallback in the request wrapper. Pseudocode:```js
if (resp.status === 401) {
  await globalRefreshLock.acquire()
  try { await maybeRefreshToken(); return client.request(original) }
  finally { globalRefreshLock.release() }
}
```

Samir Patel: We should probably fold that into SDK core to match Python behavior. Also add an opt-in "sessionLock" config so demos that run in parallel (Vercel preview builds) don't OOM.

Jordan Lee: For samplekit, maybe change demo to call the serverless API with an ephemeral bot token (rotated by template-bot) instead of using user tokens in SSR. Less friction for first-time users.

template-bot: I can add a workflow that rotates an ephemeral demo key every 12 hours and injects it as EXAMPLE_EPHEMERAL_KEY in the repo secrets for previews. Want me to do that?

Maya Chen: Yes please. That'll avoid the 401 loop for new users. Also added a note in README about the SSR token race and suggested quick-fix snippet.

Olivia Park: For the eval harness integration — did you wire retries into the prompt-eval wrapper? We need deterministic retry counts so eval pass/fail isn't flaky.

Maya Chen: I added a retry policy in the harness config: "maxRetries": 2, "backoffMs": 300, and deterministic jitter seed. It reduced flakiness on CI by ~40% locally.

Samir Patel: Excellent. Two follow-ups: 1) open SDK issue for refresh-lock + configurable retry policy, 2) patch samplekit to use the ephemeral demo key and include a small migration note for teams that copied the repo.

Jordan Lee: I can take (2) — will open PR to switch to EXAMPLE_EPHEMERAL_KEY + tiny serverless proxy that ensures 401s trigger refresh path.

deploy-bot: Deployed samplekit/next-llm-hands-on to staging (staging-templates.redwood) :rocket:

Maya Chen: Thanks — leaving a short eval checklist in the repo. If anyone runs into the SSR loop after the bot key change ping me and I'll attach logs. :thumbsup:
